# CQ 20: Which functional units are realised by no physical unit?
#
# Entries 351-56-02 and 351-56-03 keep the functional and the physical view
# apart, and realisedByPhysicalUnit joins them. A functional unit without one
# is a function nothing performs.
#
# Legitimate in one case and a gap in every other, and the class is what tells
# them apart. The controlled system, 351-49-01, is the part of the plant being
# influenced: it is the process itself rather than a device, so nothing
# realises it and nothing should. A comparing element without a device, on the
# other hand, is a function with no equipment behind it.
#
# The answer therefore needs reading rather than clearing. OWL cannot require
# the realisation, so this reports where a model has stayed silent.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?unit ?kind
WHERE {
  ?unit a ?kind . ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:FunctionalUnit .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?unit a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:FunctionalUnit }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?unit iec60050:realisedByPhysicalUnit ?any }
} ORDER BY ?kind ?unit
